<Base title="Japanese Foundations — Start Here" description="Begin Japanese with a clear, guided introduction to the writing systems, before studying hiragana and katakana." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Courses',href:'/learn/'},{label:'Japanese Foundations',href:'/learn/start/'}]}>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/learn/">Courses</a><span>›</span><span>Start here</span></nav><span class="eyebrow">LEVEL 0 · JAPANESE FOUNDATIONS</span><h1>Start with the big picture.</h1><p>New to Japanese? First learn how the language is written. Then you can approach hiragana and katakana with confidence.</p></div></section>
  <section class="page-body"><div class="container foundation-index"><div class="course-notice"><strong>Start learning today.</strong> Lessons 01–06 are published and free to study. Later Foundations lessons are still being developed.</div><span class="eyebrow">MODULE 01 · GETTING ORIENTED</span><h2>Understand the writing systems</h2><p>Learn how the scripts fit together before memorizing characters. The lesson includes explanations, original examples, an interactive check, and progress saving.</p><div class="available-lesson"><div><span class="eyebrow">LESSON 01 · ABOUT 12 MIN</span><h3>Japanese writing: a map of four systems</h3><p>Hiragana, katakana, kanji and romaji—learn what each is for.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/learn/start/module-01/chapter-01/lesson-01/">Study lesson 01 ↗</a></div><div class="available-lesson"><div><span class="eyebrow">LESSON 02 · ABOUT 22 MIN</span><h3>Japanese classroom words: read, ask, and recognize</h3><p>Script names, classroom expressions, readings versus meanings, flashcards, and interactive practice.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/learn/start/module-01/chapter-01/lesson-02/">Study lesson 02 ↗</a></div><div class="available-lesson"><div><span class="eyebrow">LESSON 03 · ABOUT 26 MIN</span><h3>How Japanese sentences work: scripts, particles and verb-final order</h3><p>Recognize は and を, the typical verb-final pattern, and polite sentence endings.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/learn/start/module-01/chapter-01/lesson-03/">Study lesson 03 ↗</a></div><div class="available-lesson"><div><span class="eyebrow">LESSON 04 · ABOUT 27 MIN</span><h3>Recognize and type your first kana</h3><p>Five hiragana/katakana vowel pairs, classroom examples, keyboard entry, and optional tracing.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/learn/start/module-01/chapter-01/lesson-04/">Study lesson 04 ↗</a></div><div class="available-lesson"><div><span class="eyebrow">LESSON 05 · ABOUT 25 MIN</span><h3>Read a Japanese script-identification chart</h3><p>Scan nine original classroom examples, locate explicit details and quote the evidence in twelve interactive questions.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/learn/start/module-01/chapter-01/lesson-05/">Study lesson 05 ↗</a></div><div class="available-lesson"><div><span class="eyebrow">LESSON 06 · ABOUT 25 MIN</span><h3>Listen to a Japanese writing-systems overview</h3><p>Two original narrated Japanese tracks, transcript-free listening, eight interactive checks and guided review.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/learn/start/module-01/chapter-01/lesson-06/">Study lesson 06 ↗</a></div><p class="foundation-next-up">Up next in the blueprint: <strong>L0-M01-C01-L07 — Writing and typing.</strong> Not published yet.</p></div></section>
